{"id": "EUVD-2026-103290", "enisaUuid": "cd5af25f-22f6-3ace-ad84-db8584a94cad", "description": "Vikunja from 2.2.0 before 2.7.0 contains a permissive CORS configuration that trusts every localhost and 127.0.0.1 port with credentials, even when service.publicurl is set. Attackers controlling a page on any localhost port can send a credentialed request to the token refresh endpoint and read the returned bearer JWT to take over the logged-in user's account.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T15:00:44", "baseScore": 7.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/go-vikunja/vikunja/security/advisories/GHSA-m687-p538-r5hp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vikunja-2.2.0-before-2.7.0-permissive-cors-policy-trusting-localhost-origins"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111922", "GHSA-r87c-f263-6pfc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f6d4788d-b394-3a03-80e3-62efa7e57142", "product": {"name": "vikunja", "vendor": {"name": "go-vikunja"}}, "product_version": "2.2.0 <2.7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "15cf4eac-c157-3e91-adf5-032dc8016602", "vendor": {"name": "go-vikunja"}}], "isExploited": false}